---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Certifications from '../components/Certifications.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const languages = [
  ['Portuguese', 'Native'],
  ['English', 'Full Professional Proficiency'],
];

/*
 * Two sources, kept apart on purpose.
 *
 * The first three are public LinkedIn recommendations, written by their
 * authors to be displayed. Verbatim, credited by name and linked to the
 * profile that carries them. The Velloso quote is trimmed; every cut is
 * marked with an ellipsis and no wording inside it was changed. Do not
 * translate these — a recommendation is the author's words, not mine.
 *
 * The rest are verbatim from the H2 2022 performance review at Caylent
 * (manager plus five peers). Attribution is by role only: the peer responses
 * were anonymous in the instrument, and the manager's answer is named in the
 * source but was written for an internal review, not for publication. Do not
 * add a name here without that person's consent, and do not invent an author
 * or a title to make a quote land harder — the manager's title was Delivery
 * Manager, not Engineering Manager.
 */
const quotes = [
  {
    quote:
      "Sergio is among the most skilled people I've ever known. He's extremely organized, he always creates a comprehensive planning before starting his activities, which gives the customer an assertive view of what has to be done and, consequently, brings expressive results. His work was essential to the success of the PCI-DSS project that we accomplished in a record time.",
    name: 'Marcelo Moreira',
    attribution: 'Principal Software Engineer',
    href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/marceloddm/',
  },
  {
    quote:
      'Sérgio is one of the best professionals that I was worked in my entire life. Always proactive and happy to solve any kind of problem that appeared. He is so obstinated to do a good job, besides he have an skill tha is fundamental to any leader, he can explain any kind of hard task in an easy way, so you can understand easy what you need to do to solve a big problem. Your knowlegment of Linux and Cloud, he is prepared to provide any kind of solution that you can ask. I endorse without any doubt Sergio to any opportunity.',
    name: 'Fernando Pereira',
    attribution: 'Senior Site Reliability Engineer',
    href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/fernando-pereira-br/',
  },
  {
    quote:
      'Sérgio é um profissional que tive o privilégio de conhecer e trabalhar junto. […] Possui uma visão extremamente abrangente da TI e suas nuances que convergem num profissional extremamente completo capaz de entregar projetos de grande complexidade em prazos acordados e superar os objetivos sob seus cuidados. […] Sua experiência em arquitetura de infraestrutura de TI permitiram a empresa que atuamos juntos alçar novos patamares no desenvolvimento, na prestação e robustez de seus serviços.',
    name: 'Thiago Velloso',
    attribution: 'Security Specialist',
    href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/thiago-velloso-85535b54/',
  },
  {
    quote:
      'Sergio has a high say:do ratio. He consistently completes the assigned work in the allocated time and always comes prepared for customer meetings with the necessary architecture diagrams and slides.',
    attribution: 'Peer review, Caylent, 2022',
  },
  {
    quote:
      "Sergio has the ability to see the overall design on a project and deliver technically. He's good at circling back to see the bigger picture, and yet play Jira stories when needed to write code or deploy infra.",
    attribution: 'Peer review, Caylent, 2022',
  },
  {
    quote:
      'It is rare to see such selfless leadership from an architect in my experience.',
    attribution: 'Peer review, Caylent, 2022',
  },
  {
    quote:
      'He had to develop a strong understanding of their Machine Learning stack, which is not in his background. He dove in and learned what he had to complete the migration.',
    attribution: 'Delivery Manager, Caylent, 2022',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Sérgio Francisco — infrastructure engineer in Rio de Janeiro. Bio, how I work, what colleagues said, certifications and education."
>
  <section class="border-b border-border">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[52rem] px-6 pt-16 pb-10 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h1 class="display mt-4 text-[30px] sm:text-[38px]">Sérgio Francisco</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[52rem] px-6 py-12 sm:px-8">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am an infrastructure engineer. The market splits that into DevOps, Site
        Reliability Engineer, Platform Engineer and Cloud Architect, and I have
        delivered as each of them. Underneath it all I am a sysadmin who kept up
        with the market.
      </p>
      <p>
        Seventeen years, starting in September 2008 as an IT intern at RNP. Six of
        those years running Kubernetes in production across EKS, AKS and GKE — from
        a 30-cluster global fleet to GitOps delivery with Argo CD, Flux and Helm
        charts written in-house. Most of what I am good at is turning an ambiguous
        production problem into something shipped and measurable, and building the
        tooling that keeps other teams' services reliable.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work from Rio de Janeiro, in {site.timezone} — full overlap with US
        East.
      </p>

    </div>

    <h2 class="label pt-14">How I work</h2>
    <div class="prose pt-6">
      <p>
        I do my best work with a clear goal and room to run. Tell me what has to
        be true and by when, and I will come back with the architecture, the
        trade-offs I rejected on the way, and a date I intend to hold.
      </p>
      <p>
        I write before I build. A diagram or a short design document is how I
        find the problem I actually have — and it gives the team something to
        argue with now, rather than arguing with my code three weeks later. I
        would rather be corrected on a page than in production.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="label pt-14">What colleagues said</h2>
    <ul class="mt-6 border-t border-border">
      {quotes.map(({ quote, attribution, name, href }) => (
        <li
          class={
            name
              ? 'border-b border-border py-6 sm:py-8'
              : 'border-b border-border py-5 sm:py-6'
          }
        >
          <blockquote
            class={
              name
                ? 'max-w-[62ch] text-[15px] text-[#cfd2d6] italic sm:text-[16px]'
                : 'max-w-[62ch] text-[#cfd2d6] italic'
            }
          >
            &ldquo;{quote}&rdquo;
          </blockquote>
          {name ? (
            <p class="mt-3 text-[13px] text-faint">
              <a
                class="link-quiet text-text hover:decoration-muted"
                href={href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                {name}
              </a>
              {' \u2014 '}
              {attribution}
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p class="mt-2 text-[12px] text-faint">{attribution}</p>
          )}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2 class="label pt-14">Certifications</h2>
    <Certifications />

    <div class="prose pt-6">
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Faculdade de Informática Lemos de Castro</strong> — Bachelor of
        Science in Information Systems, 2007–2010.
      </p>

      <h2>Languages</h2>
      <ul>
        {languages.map(([name, level]) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{name}</strong> — {level}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={site.github} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>{' · '}<a
          href={site.linkedin}
          rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a
        >{' · '}<a href={site.resume} rel="noopener">Résumé</a>{' · '}<a
          href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
